  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "eugr's (Eugene Rakhmatulin) spark-vllm-docker nemotron-3-super-nvfp4 recipe for NVIDIA's NVIDIA-Nemotron-3-Super-120B-A12B-NVFP4 (NVIDIA Nemotron Open Model License; checkpoint revision ff433f54) served by vLLM on two Sparks. Runs eugr's published vllm-node image (nightly-20260929, digest pinned; its build-metadata records spark-vllm-docker 42f62e34, vLLM 0.30.1rc1.dev336+gaf5b4857e and FlashInfer 4a638133) with upstream's launch: CUTLASS MoE backend, TRITON_ATTN attention, FP8 KV cache, float32 mamba SSM cache, InstantTensor loading, prefix caching, qwen3_coder tool-call parser, nemotron_v3 reasoning parser, 262,144-token context, ten sequences and memory utilisation 0.8 (upstream defaults), with VLLM_FLASHINFER_ALLREDUCE_BACKEND=trtllm and VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN=1. Tensor parallel 2 across the pair uses vLLM's native multi-node launch, eugr's default no-Ray cluster mode, so upstream's --distributed-executor-backend ray is dropped. The 80 GB checkpoint fits one Spark, so both topologies apply. No upstream performance claims are recorded. Upstream repository MIT. Physical Spark acceptance is pending.",
